  35:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/StatisticsFunctions/arm_rms_q15.c **** 
  36:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/StatisticsFunctions/arm_rms_q15.c **** /**
  37:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/StatisticsFunctions/arm_rms_q15.c ****  * @brief Root Mean Square of the elements of a Q15 vector.
  38:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/StatisticsFunctions/arm_rms_q15.c ****  * @param[in]       *pSrc points to the input vector
  39:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/StatisticsFunctions/arm_rms_q15.c ****  * @param[in]       blockSize length of the input vector
  40:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/StatisticsFunctions/arm_rms_q15.c ****  * @param[out]      *pResult rms value returned here
  41:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/StatisticsFunctions/arm_rms_q15.c ****  * @return none.
  42:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/StatisticsFunctions/arm_rms_q15.c ****  *
  43:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/StatisticsFunctions/arm_rms_q15.c ****  * @details
  44:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/StatisticsFunctions/arm_rms_q15.c ****  * <b>Scaling and Overflow Behavior:</b>
  45:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/StatisticsFunctions/arm_rms_q15.c ****  *
  46:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/StatisticsFunctions/arm_rms_q15.c ****  * \par
  47:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/StatisticsFunctions/arm_rms_q15.c ****  * The function is implemented using a 64-bit internal accumulator.
  48:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/StatisticsFunctions/arm_rms_q15.c ****  * The input is represented in 1.15 format.
  49:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/StatisticsFunctions/arm_rms_q15.c ****  * Intermediate multiplication yields a 2.30 format, and this
  50:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/StatisticsFunctions/arm_rms_q15.c ****  * result is added without saturation to a 64-bit accumulator in 34.30 format.
  51:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/StatisticsFunctions/arm_rms_q15.c ****  * With 33 guard bits in the accumulator, there is no risk of overflow, and the
  52:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/StatisticsFunctions/arm_rms_q15.c ****  * full precision of the intermediate multiplication is preserved.
  53:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/StatisticsFunctions/arm_rms_q15.c ****  * Finally, the 34.30 result is truncated to 34.15 format by discarding the lower
  54:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/StatisticsFunctions/arm_rms_q15.c ****  * 15 bits, and then saturated to yield a result in 1.15 format.
  55:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/StatisticsFunctions/arm_rms_q15.c ****  *
  56:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/StatisticsFunctions/arm_rms_q15.c ****  */
  57:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/StatisticsFunctions/arm_rms_q15.c **** 
  58:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/StatisticsFunctions/arm_rms_q15.c **** void arm_rms_q15(
  59:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/StatisticsFunctions/arm_rms_q15.c ****   q15_t * pSrc,
  60:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/StatisticsFunctions/arm_rms_q15.c ****   uint32_t blockSize,
  61:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/StatisticsFunctions/arm_rms_q15.c ****   q15_t * pResult)
